t both, and the executor applies it and emits the reply; no message was prepared by hand, which is what distinguishes this check from the attempt recorded last turn. Oracle and identity: the observation is the bytes written to the client's reply writer together with the new instance's statuses, and the applicability condition ties the reply event to the admitted operation through the instance identity. Contrary evidence and limits: the harness supplies the reply writer rather than a socket, so it observes bytes the implementation wrote; one operation and one re-proposal round are exercised; and the case where the admitting replica is lost remains out of scope (its proposal is never transmitted, as the earlier codec and client reads showed). No counterevidence was found that the operation is dropped in this scope.\\\",\n  \\\"limitations\\\":[\\\"the client's reply writer is supplied by the harness, so the check observes written bytes rather than a socket\\\",\n   \\\"one operation and one re-proposal round are exercised\\\",\n   \\\"the case where the admitting replica is lost is out of scope and stays with the paused client-retry question\\\"]}]}\njson.dump(sub,open('submission-review-c5b.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nprint('ok')\nPY\ncd .. && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run --submission submission-review-c5b.json 2>&1 | head -6\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
